e/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/gemini-robotics-er-2/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Steven Hansen</name><title>Senior Staff Software Engineer</title><department/><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Peng Xu</name><title>Staff Software Engineer</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Take a look at short films created by our latest group of artists in Google’s Flow Sessions program.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/google-flow-sessions-short-films/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Flow_social_A.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Flow_social_A.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re sharing a look at the short films created by our latest group of artists in Google’s Flow Sessions program.</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/google-flow-sessions-short-films/</guid><category>Google Labs</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Take a look at short films created by our latest group of artists in Google’s Flow Sessions program.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/google-flow-sessions-short-films/</url></og></item><item><title>How the Head of YouTube Health handles screen time with his kids</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/families/kids-summer-screen-time-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Screentime_Hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Colorful illustration of two smiling parents and a child holding a tablet.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Screentime_Hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Hear from Dr. Garth Graham on how he sets rules in his own home and helpful approaches for communicating about screen time.</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/families/kids-summer-screen-time-tips/</guid><category>Families</category><category>YouTube</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>How the Head of YouTube Health handles screen time with his kids</title><description>Hear from Dr. Garth Graham on how he sets rules in his own home and helpful approaches for communicating about screen time.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/families/kids-summer-screen-time-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Joel Meares</name><title>Contributor</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>We’re launching Lyria 3.5 in Google Flow Music, with advances across musicality, lyrics, vocals, and creative control.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/lyria-3-5/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Lyria3.5_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Lyria3.5_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Our newest music generation model, Lyria 3.5, delivers significant advancements across musicality, lyrics, and vocal quality, empowering you to craft richer tracks. We’r…</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/lyria-3-5/</guid><category>Google DeepMind</category><category>Google Labs</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>We’re launching Lyria 3.5 in Google Flow Music, with advances across musicality, lyrics, vocals, and creative control.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/lyria-3-5/</url></og></item><item><title>Gemini API Managed Agents: 3.6 Flash, hooks, and more</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api-3-6-flash-hooks/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/unnamed_2_vNnOv20.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Managed Agents Gemini 3.6 Flash, Hooks and Triggers</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/unnamed_2_vNnOv20.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re announcing even more new capabilities in Managed Agents in Gemini API so developers can build reliable, production-ready agents.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api-3-6-flash-hooks/</guid><category>Developer tools</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Gemini API Managed Agents: 3.6 Flash, hooks, and more</title><description>We’re announcing even more new capabilities in Managed Agents in Gemini API so developers can build reliable, production-ready agents.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api-3-6-flash-hooks/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Philipp Schmid</name><title>Member of the Technical Staff</title><department>Google DeepMind</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Mariano Cocirio</name><title>Product Manager</title><department>Google DeepMind</department><company/></author></item><item><title>5 ways AI Mode in Search helps you enjoy the real world</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-real-world-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/AI_Mode_real_world.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Illustration of a black magnifying glass in a white circle on green grass surrounded by items related to fun activities like tennis and games</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/AI_Mode_real_world.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;It might sound counterintuitive, but Search's AI tools can actually help you make the most of your time offline whether you want to book concert tickets or find the perf…</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-real-world-tips/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>5 ways AI Mode in Search helps you enjoy the real world</title><description>It might sound counterintuitive, but Search's AI tools can actually help you make the most of your time offline whether you want to book concert tickets or find the perfect hiking boots.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-real-world-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>5 ways to host the ultimate dinner party with Google Search</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Dinner_parties.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>An illustrated black magnifying glass with a sparkle in a white circle surrounded by a dinner party tablescape</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Dinner_parties.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;These AI features can help you craft a menu, design a tablescape, and handle other party-planning tasks.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>5 ways to host the ultimate dinner party with Google Search</title><description>These AI features can help you craft a menu, design a tablescape, and handle other party-planning tasks.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Google and KDDI are ready to back Japanese startups.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/ai-startup-support-program-japan/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Google_AI_Futures_Fund__KDDI_ba.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Google_AI_Futures_Fund__KDDI_ba.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re launching the AI Startup Support Program to accelerate innovative AI-native Japanese startups.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 01:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/ai-startup-support-program-japan/</guid><category>Google Labs</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Google and KDDI are ready to back Japanese startups.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/ai-startup-support-program-japan/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Jonathan Silber</name><title>Co-Founder &amp; Director</title><department>Google AI Futures Fund</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Understanding the AI economy</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/research/understanding-the-ai-economy/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/hero_image_3_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>"AI &amp; Economy Atlas" with Google logo, all over a green grid background</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/hero_image_3_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re releasing the first Activity, Task, Landscape, and Adoption Study (ATLAS) report, showing how people use Google’s AI tools.</description><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/research/understanding-the-ai-economy/</guid><category>Google Research</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Understanding the AI economy</title><description>We’re releasing the first Activity, Task, Landscape, and Adoption Study (ATLAS) report, showing how people use Google’s AI tools.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/research/understanding-the-ai-economy/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Zanna Iscenko</name><title>AI &amp; Economy Lead</title><department>Chief Economist's Office</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Scott Strand</name><title>Head of StratOps and Special Projects</title><department>Technology &amp; Society</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Introducing selfie for sign-in: a new, easy way to access your Google Account</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/safety-security/selfie-video-sign-in/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Selfie_sign-in_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Sizzle video overviewing using selfie video to verify identity</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Selfie_sign-in_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Selfie video gives you more options if you’re ever locked out or don’t have access to your usual phone or computer.</description><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/safety-security/selfie-video-sign-in/</guid><category>Safety &amp; Security</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Introducing selfie for sign-in: a new, easy way to access your Google Account</title><description>Selfie video gives you more options if you’re ever locked out or don’t have access to your usual phone or computer.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/safety-security/selfie-video-sign-in/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>John Gronberg</name><title>Director, Product Management</title><department/><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Claire Forszt</name><title>Product Manager, Google Identity and Engagement</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>3 Google updates from Galaxy Unpacked 2026</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/galaxy-unpacked-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Unpacked_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Gentle Monster glasses, Warby Parker glasses, a prompt asking for the history behind a pictured building, and a prompt asking to book a table at a pictured restaurant</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Unpacked_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We shared how Samsung users can boost productivity and get time back on new foldables, watches, and glasses coming soon.</description><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/galaxy-unpacked-2026/</guid><category>Gemini App</category><category>Android</category><category>Gemini Notebook</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>3 Google updates from Galaxy Unpacked 2026</title><description>We shared how Samsung users can boost productivity and get time back on new foldables, watches, and glasses coming soon.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/galaxy-unpacked-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Menaka Shroff</name><title>VP of Android Ecosystem Marketing</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Connect more of your apps to Search</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ConnectedAppshero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Connected apps rendering</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ConnectedAppshero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;You’ll be able to securely link and interact with your go-to services directly in AI Mode.</description><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Connect more of your apps to Search</title><description>You’ll be able to securely link and interact with your go-to services directly in AI Mode.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Chips Mistry</name><title>Senior Product Manager</title><department>Search</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Biharck Araújo</name><title>Engineering Lead</title><department>Search</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Create, edit and star in videos with two Google Vids updates</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/gemini-omni-personal-avatars/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/omni-blog-header_OarEe2t.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Text "Gemini Omni and Personal Avatars in Google Vids" surrounded by various images</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/omni-blog-header_OarEe2t.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Gemini Omni and personal avatars in Google Vids make video creation easier than ever.</description><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/gemini-omni-personal-avatars/</guid><category>Google Workspace</category><category>Google One</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Create, edit and star in videos with two Google Vids updates</title><description>Gemini Omni and personal avatars in Google Vids make video creation easier than ever.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/gemini-omni-personal-avatars/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Justin Luk</name><title>Product Manager</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Celebrating 25 years of visual search innovation</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-images-25th-anniversary/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Google_Images_25th_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Google Images logo surrounded by illustrations of people searching for different images</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Google_Images_25th_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google Images is turning 25. Here’s a look back at some major milestones — and new ways to explore and create visual content.</description><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-images-25th-anniversary/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Celebrating 25 years of visual search innovation</title><description>Google Images is turning 25. Here’s a look back at some major milestones — and new ways to explore and create visual content.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-images-25th-anniversary/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Brad Kellett</name><title>Senior Engineering Director</title><department>Search</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Reconstructing Pelé’s “lost” goal</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/reconstructing-peles-lost-goal/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Screenshot_2026-07-13_at_7.18.4.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Pele documentary</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Screenshot_2026-07-13_at_7.18.4.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;See how Google DeepMind AI technology reconstructed Pelé’s legendary 1959 lost goal at Rua Javari in our new mini-documentary.</description><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/reconstructing-peles-lost-goal/</guid><category>Google in Latin America</category><category>Google DeepMind</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Reconstructing Pelé’s “lost” goal</title><description>See how Google DeepMind AI technology reconstructed Pelé’s legendary 1959 lost goal at Rua Javari in our new mini-documentary.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/reconstructing-peles-lost-goal/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Anita Lucchesi</name><title>Brazilian Historian</title><department>UERJ &amp; Arka</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Gabe Ferreira</name><title>Google Creative Lead</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>We're rolling out AlphaEvolve widely to solve Google Cloud customers' hardest problems.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/infrastructure-and-cloud/google-cloud/alphaevolve-on-cloud/</link><media:c